openssh-pkcs11: ML-DSA and SLH-DSA for OpenSSH through PKCS#11
==============================================================

This folder patches and builds OpenSSH portable,
https://github.com/openssh/openssh-portable, tag V_10_3_P1
(commit 2d98db98331803cbb820211b2fb0d31a6e71e58e), fetched by
scripts/build-wasm.sh. OpenSSH is distributed under the terms in LICENSE in
this folder, which is the LICENCE file of that OpenSSH release, unchanged.
Those terms cover OpenSSH and every OpenSSH file changed by this folder.

Changes by PQC Today, LLC (2026)
--------------------------------
patches/apply_mldsa_patches.py edits these OpenSSH files at build time:
  Makefile.in, myproposal.h, sshkey.h, sshkey.c, ssh-pkcs11.c,
  sshd-auth.c, sshd.c
It registers the ssh-mldsa-44/65/87 and ssh-slh-dsa-* key types, adds
ML-DSA/SLH-DSA signing through PKCS#11 (CKM_ML_DSA, CKM_SLH_DSA), and adds the
new objects to the build. The changes to OpenSSH files are under the OpenSSH
terms in LICENSE.

New files written by PQC Today, LLC, compiled into the build or used to make
it: patches/ssh-mldsa.c, patches/ssh-slhdsa.c, patches/native_paramsweep_test.c,
patches/apply_mldsa_patches.py, wasm-shims/*.c, scripts/*.sh, *.cjs. They are
written against OpenSSH's internal interfaces and are provided under the
BSD 2-Clause terms below. Where they follow OpenSSH's own code (for example
the user-authentication request layout in wasm-shims/sshd_wasm_main.c), the
OpenSSH terms in LICENSE apply to those parts as well.

